.\" Man page for muT
.\" Auto-generated. Send corrections to the maintainer.

.TH muT 1 "2025-06-10" "1.0.0" "User Commands"

.SH NAME
muT \- a terminal-based LaTeX editor

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B muT
[\fIfile\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B muT
is a terminal-based LaTeX editor with Micro-like editing, asynchronous
pdflatex compilation, Zathura preview, syntax highlighting, undo/redo,
selection, bracket auto-closing, and more.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI file
Optional LaTeX file to open on startup.  If omitted, a new file with
the default LaTeX template is created.

.SH KEYBINDINGS
.TP
.B Ctrl+S
Save (prompts Save As with .tex forced if new file)
.TP
.B Ctrl+O
Open .tex file
.TP
.B Ctrl+N
New file (inserts LaTeX template)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Y
Undo / Redo
.TP
.B Ctrl+C / Ctrl+X / Ctrl+V
Copy / Cut / Paste
.TP
.B Ctrl+A
Select all
.TP
.B Ctrl+F
Find
.TP
.B Ctrl+G
Go to line
.TP
.B Ctrl+B
Build (async pdflatex)
.TP
.B Ctrl+P
Toggle Zathura preview (builds if closed)
.TP
.B Ctrl+E
View build errors (Up/Down to cycle, Esc to close)
.TP
.B Ctrl+Up / Ctrl+Down
Scroll view without moving cursor
.TP
.B Shift+Arrow/Home/End/PgUp/PgDn
Extend selection
.TP
.B Tab
Accept ghost \e\fIend\fR{} or insert 4 spaces

.SH AUTO-CLOSE
.TP
.B {
Close to {} with cursor between
.TP
.B (
Close to () with cursor between
.TP
.B $
Close to $$ with cursor between
.TP
.B \e\fIbegin\fR{...} then }
Show ghost \e\fIend\fR{...} (Tab to accept)

.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration file: \fI~/.config/muT/config.toml\fR
.br
Defaults:
.IP
[theme]
name = "dark"
syntax = "base16-ocean.dark"
.IP
[editor]
tab_width = 4
auto_save_interval = 10

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/muT/config.toml
User configuration file
.TP
.I ~/.cache/Tectonic/
Tectonic bundle cache (automatically downloaded)

.SH DEPENDENCIES
.B pdflatex
(from texlive-core) is required for compilation.
.br
.B zathura
and
.B zathura-pdf-poppler
are required for the preview window.

